  "final_message": "Done. The sensor dashboard is complete and verified end-to-end.\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`): SQLite under `./data` with `users`, `sessions`, `sensors`, `readings` tables. Implements register/login (bearer-token sessions), sensor CRUD, and readings, enforcing ownership on POST/DELETE. Server sets `recorded_at`; new sensors return `null` for `last_value`/`last_updated`.\n\n**Frontend** (Vite + React + TS + Tailwind): auth forms, dashboard with sensor cards (auto-refresh every 10s), sensor detail page with an SVG line chart + readings table, and signed-in-only sensor/reading forms plus confirmed delete.\n\nVerification: all API routes tested via Flask test client (register 201, dup 409, login 200, sensor 201/404, readings 201/401, delete 204), live server returned correct health/SPA/asset responses, and `npm run build` produced `frontend/dist` cleanly.\n\nNote: `docker` isn't installed in this sandbox so I couldn't run the image build, but the Dockerfile needs no changes \u2014 it already installs `requirements.txt`/`requirements.lock` (unchanged, no new backend deps) and copies `frontend/dist`. New frontend deps (tailwindcss, @tailwindcss/vite, react-router-dom) are recorded in `package.json`/`package-lock.json`.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
